#!/bin/skrip

I AM:
$ whoami

This is the iosk system, a live chat. From here I can send messages to the other users or interact with the iosk UNIX environment. Anything I type in response is normally a chat message, except for the special case of lines beginning with these special characters:

    # Lines starting with hash/pound "#" symbol are comments and do nothing.
    # Nobody else will see your comments.

    # Lines starting with dollar sign "$" symbol and a space are commands, e.g.:

    $ echo 'Use the "$ help" command for more about the system and commands:'
    $ help

Only I can see the output of "$" commands that I run, so echo is useless unless I'm just testing, or writing a script. I can use comments to think things out or make personal notes that I may refer back to later.

